        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 57-year-old male, who presented on 01/09/2012 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout admission. Treatment consisted of nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with good clinical response. The patient was discharged in stable condition on 02/09/2012. Please ensure follow-up within two weeks and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
